WEBVTT

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.610
About the investigation being conducted 
on Jin Makata’s blank year...

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.490
At this point in time,

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.690
I have only been able to catch 
bits and pieces of his trail.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.620
“Puzzles are chains. 
Puzzles are mirrors,” huh?

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.500
Sir?

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.230
A report came in from Kaito.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.500
It mentions how Raetsel told him that.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.260
We still don’t know 
anything about her...

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.020
Rook, do you really think it’s 
okay for puzzles to exist?

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:47.580
Are you... happy to have 
encountered puzzles?

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:24.010
I Get that Feeling

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.250
Sheesh... I don’t know what to think!

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.750
You’re talking about 
Raetsel, aren’t you?

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.030
The Jin I knew was the one true Jin!

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.010
Your Jin was just some fraud!

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.200
Her eyes were serious.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.010
I don’t think she was telling a lie.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.540
Yeah, same here.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.750
But if that’s the case, what about 
her claim that Jin hates puzzles?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.640
Is that also true?

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.880
That’s not even a possibility!

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:57.050
Dammit! What the heck is going on here?

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.900
We’ll have to search for 
the answer to that ourselves.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:01.910
Rook!

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.140
What a crappy puzzle!

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.910
It’s not even worthy 
of our hate, is it?

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.460
That brooch...

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.470
By any chance, did I...?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.870
Did you remember?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.790
No... It’s just, I got that feeling...

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:31.940
I was so totally right when I 
decided to wear this brooch!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.330
I had a hunch it might 
jog your memories!

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.570
Why don’t you come with me after all?

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.670
It might help your memories come back!

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.700
B-but...

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.950
Don’t you want to remember your past?

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.700
Then it’s settled!

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:54.260
I’ll come pick you 
up later, so sit tight!

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.120
Prepare to welcome Jin onboard?

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:06.580
Naturally, I’d be happy to 
welcome our leader with open arms,

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.200
but weren’t you going to leave him

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.480
with Kaito Daimon until 
he regained his memories?

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.210
Was I? Doesn’t ring a bell!

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.990
I swear, you are such a naughty kitten.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:37.750
Director Rook wanted to 
speak with Raetsel...?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.650
Right. Kaito is with them.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.150
Where’d they go?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.880
Well, he wanted to keep it a 
private conversation, so...

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.140
And leave us out?!

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.370
There is no need to worry, Cubik.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.270
It was the director’s idea.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.330
I have no doubt that he 
knows what he is doing.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.620
But still...!

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.250
I, Ana, am worried...

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.280
Yeah! It’s dangerous for 
them to be alone with Raetsel!

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.400
No, I’m not worried about her.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.340
Ever since she showed up, Kaito has...

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.970
I, Ana, feel like Kaito has 
reverted to when we first met.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.040
When you first met?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.040
Back to when Kaito loved 
puzzles, yet hated them...

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.420
So, what’s Jin up to?

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.550
He is in his room. Is there a problem?

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.410
Not really.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.990
Kaito...

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.810
Here. This one is for you.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.870
I don’t want any!

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.690
This isn’t why you 
called me here, is it?

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.500
They taste best when 
they’re still hot!

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.260
You see, this is a rare treat for me.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:49.070
Didn’t you want to 
talk to me about Jin?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.080
Oh, yeah! So, Rook, what 
did you wanna tell us?

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:59.210
You, me and Jin used to play 
puzzles together, didn’t we?

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.460
Yeah, we sure did...

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.840
There is no way...

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.660
I could see Jin ever say 
that he hates puzzles.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:19.520
But, Raetsel, I don’t think 
you’re lying to us, either.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.540
Of course not.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:26.130
Wasn’t there once a time, Kaito, 
when you hated puzzles yourself?

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.610
A puzzle took your parents’ 
lives, didn’t it?

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.190
Jin told me about what happened, Kaito.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.730
You, too, harbor a hatred for puzzles.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.880
So how could you say that Jin doesn’t?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.130
Same for you, Rook.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.060
After you were devoured 
by the Armlet of Orpheus,

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.780
you created one dangerous 
puzzle after the next.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.520
You may... be absolutely right.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.020
“Is it truly all right 
for puzzles to exist?”

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.940
To be honest, Jin asked me that 
question once in the past.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.070
Rook?

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:11.160
And then, Jin continued by saying,

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:14.840
“Puzzles are chains. 
Puzzles are mirrors.”

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:21.100
That’s the exact same 
thing Jin told Raetsel...

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.420
He said it to me as well.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.220
It was word-for-word the same.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.420
So what of it?

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.650
This took place on a summer day.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:35.180
I just so happened to 
be alone with Jin...

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:40.680
Rook, do you really think it’s 
okay for puzzles to exist?

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:47.320
Are you... happy to have 
encountered puzzles?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.190
They’re fun...

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:55.050
There may be sad puzzles... 
as well as terrifying puzzles.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.450
Even so--Even so, they’re fun!

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.100
There is no such thing 
as an unwanted puzzle!

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.330
And even if there was, I’m sure that 
it would be the human creator’s fault!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.310
You’re right. I’m sorry, my bad!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.490
Sometimes I find you looking 
lonesome, you know?

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.120
I was simply asking that weird 
question out of concern.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.450
I’m sorry.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.870
But, yes, you’re 
absolutely right, Rook!

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.920
Everything depends on us humans.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.630
Puzzles are chains. 
Puzzles are also mirrors.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.170
They’re chains and mirrors?

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:34.490
What does that mean?

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.560
That’s a puzzle in and of itself.

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:43.120
I still don’t know the 
answer to that puzzle.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.380
Puzzles bind people,

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:47.900
reflecting aspects of ourselves 
that we never wanted to see.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.380
That’s what Jin was trying to say.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.630
Is that... really what he meant to say?

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:56.970
I was with Jin all the time!

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.540
I know him inside and out!

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.270
Then... how about this?

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.770
Youngster X!

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.540
So Jin made that puzzle?

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.640
Jin!

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.930
Are you making a puzzle?

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:23.430
Will you punish the puzzlers with it?

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:27.190
Dunno. What do you think?

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.800
How did you get that puzzle...?

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:35.320
I looked into Jin’s blank year.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:41.060
In other words, I traced the footsteps 
you took together with Jin.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:44.160
The pieces of data on Jin’s 
journey that are still intact...

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:49.560
depict a brutal series of heroic 
battles against the Puzzles of Fools.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.440
But that wasn’t all I found.

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:01.120
I stumbled upon this: A photo 
that appeared in a newspaper.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:06.110
Amidst his difficult 
battles, Jin was trying to

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:08.560
teach children how much 
fun puzzles can be!

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:10.630
You’re lying!

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.980
You photoshopped that picture!

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.140
Jin planted a trap in that puzzle with

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.300
the intent of punishing puzzlers who...

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.510
I’m not finding any traps in this.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.660
It’s a good, warm puzzle.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.290
Jin truly is the man 
I--we knew him to be.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.520
The Puzzles of Fools and the children...

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:36.280
The two may have caused 
Jin’s heart to waver.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:40.360
That might be why he asked you if

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.870
it’s all right for 
puzzles to exist, Rook.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:45.410
I-I don’t buy it!

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:50.150
We don’t know everything 
about Jin, nor do you.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.860
“Hate puzzlers.”

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:54.400
I guess Jin could have told you that.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.490
But on the flip side...

00:10:56.490 --> 00:11:00.300
Right. He may have had reasons 
we didn’t know about.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.580
Could you help us find out 
what they were, Raetsel?

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:07.120
If the three of us work together, 
we can uncover Jin’s past--

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.560
we’ll reach the heart of the matter!

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:13.760
K-keep dreaming! Kaito 
Daimon, you hated puzzles.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:18.820
Rook Banjo Crossfield, you 
created murderous puzzles!

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.320
Jin hated puzzles, too!

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.070
That’s the truth!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:26.060
I will not deny my past,

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:29.960
but I will not allow anyone to 
decide Jin’s past for him.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.710
Excuse me?!

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.530
Fine! In that case, 
I’ll show it to you.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.970
I’ll let you see the most loathsome 
puzzle Jin ever showed me.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.580
It’s the most terrifying 
puzzle in the world!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.380
Kaito never did come back...

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.760
Jin, what are you up to?

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:06.030
These puzzles... What 
do you think of them?

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:09.410
Are these puzzles... lousy?

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.940
Well, I’m not the best person to ask.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:17.590
I’m horrible at puzzles.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.170
Are you really?

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:22.450
Uh, but, well, these 
puzzles are kinda cute,

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.550
so I bet they’d be fun to solve...

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:40.800
This is a Puzzle of Fools?

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.490
I never knew there was one here!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:44.470
As far as I’m aware, this is the

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:47.350
most dangerous and treacherous 
puzzle in the world.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.620
It was bad enough that even Jin 
gave up on setting it free.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:52.870
Jin did?!

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.230
Jin hated and feared this puzzled.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.770
That is the truth.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.780
Rook Banjo Crossfield, if you don’t

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.880
believe me, why don’t 
you give it a shot?

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:04.500
All right.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:05.630
Rook!

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:09.580
“Puzzles are chains. 
Puzzles are also mirrors.”

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.890
I want to learn the truth 
behind those words.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:16.080
If I challenge the same 
puzzle that Jin faced,

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:18.290
it may bring me closer to 
understanding how Jin felt.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:32.270
So that’s the goal?

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:46.010
With a bottomless pit blow 
me, there is nowhere to run.

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:50.240
But there are sharp 
spears waiting for me...

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.390
if I try to force my way 
across the different pillars.

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.790
In other words, if I 
want to reach the exit,

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.040
I have no choice but 
to solve this puzzle.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:07.530
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:14.640
I see. When I step onto a stone 
pillar, its height changes.

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:16.790
So then these numbers are...

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:23.670
Each of the stone pillars 
is assigned a number.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:28.300
The numbers on the tablet Rook is 
holding are supposed to serve as a hint.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:32.170
The first stone pillar was 14.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.990
Next was 46.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.310
I suspect that the numbers represent 
their original height...

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:40.040
and how high they will go.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.400
Then what about the pillars 
with only one number?

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.170
Rook!

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:01.670
That was close! If he 
hadn’t gotten off...!

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:06.610
Single-digit numbers rise.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.050
They crash into the ceiling, 
making them dead ends.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.080
And to top it off,

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.560
there is a limit to how long 
I may stand on each pillar.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:19.780
If I go forward to 32, I’ll be forced 
to go on the single-digit pillar, 2.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.020
I should head for 35.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.940
Looks like he’s figured out the rules.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.520
Rook...

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.460
Just as you lost your parents,

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.920
you might lose your best 
friend to a puzzle.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:54.150
A long time ago, this puzzle stole my...

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.180
That puzzle...

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:08.570
That puzzle was so scary 
that I couldn’t solve it.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:13.070
That was the only puzzle 
I was unable to solve.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:15.010
You too?

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:20.310
Yeah! That is the most terrifying 
Puzzle of Fools I’ve ever seen.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:22.020
Is that right?

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.260
Raetsel, don’t go near 
that dangerous puzzle

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.350
all by yourself ever again!

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:28.940
But I wanna help you--

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:29.860
Here.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:32.970
What’s this?

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:35.160
My good luck charm.

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:37.220
I’d like you to keep it from now on.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:40.830
When I’m challenging 
a Puzzle of Fools,

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:43.330
please pray for my 
safety and wait for me.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:52.610
Puzzles stole Jin’s 
gentle smile from me!

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:05.020
Next, I’ll have to take 
either pillar 6 or 61.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.110
But if I take 6...

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:12.140
The single-digit pillars 
crash into the ceiling.

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:15.080
So I’ll take 61.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:20.390
No. If I take 61, I won’t 
be able to progress.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:27.330
In other words, I can’t 
go beyond this point.

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:31.580
Does this puzzle lack an answer?!

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:37.870
Now do you get it?

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:41.410
Puzzles are vile things that 
steal the ones we hold dear.

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:45.230
Kaito, a puzzle is going 
to steal from you again.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:47.600
This time, it’s going 
to be your dear friend.

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:48.920
You’re wrong.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.370
Can’t you hear it?

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.920
This Puzzle of Fools is crying.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.680
The puzzle is crying?

00:17:57.240 --> 00:18:01.430
Back when I solved the puzzle 
that took my mom and dad,

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:03.870
I heard it then, too.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.060
I could hear the sound of the puzzle 
rejoicing when I set it free.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.570
It’s not like this became a killer 
puzzle because it wanted to.

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:17.830
It’s not the puzzle’s fault, 
but the person who made the puzzle!

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:22.310
Rook! Listen to the voice of the puzzle!

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:26.830
And free this puzzle from its agony!

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:31.960
Right... You’re right, Kaito.

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:36.610
Don’t be afraid. Face the puzzle!

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.830
A piece of the tablet is on 6’s floor.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:47.850
Which means...

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:53.480
I...

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.690
believe in you!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.360
Rook!

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:06.140
Cool! Some of the stone 
pillars go down instead!

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:10.940
Next I should jump onto 5--No, 3!

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.690
But if 3 descends, I’ll go to 12.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:14.980
If 12 rises, I’ll take...

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:17.420
78!

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:21.490
Sweet!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.520
Im-impossible!

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:24.430
He overcame such a tough spot!

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.060
Great! I’m almost there.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.470
N-no way...!

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:43.950
Dang, you had me worried sick.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.900
Jin, as well as you, Kaito...

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:57.460
The two of you saved me.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:58.840
Me and Jin?

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:03.470
For a minute, I couldn’t decide 
which stone pillar to jump onto.

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:06.700
I’m not sure if he did 
it intentionally or not,

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:11.810
but I think that was there from 
when Jin freed the puzzle.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:13.890
You’re making crap up!

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:15.880
Jin told me that he couldn’t solve--

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.570
He lied to you.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:20.730
I bet he didn’t want you getting

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.090
anywhere near this dangerous puzzle.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:24.900
Kaito’s voice...

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:29.020
and the hint Jin left behind 
dispelled my hesitation.

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.770
It finally makes sense to me now.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.780
Puzzles are chains.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:37.840
Chains are bonds that tightly 
link people together.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:40.240
They link people together?

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:43.780
Aren’t you linked to 
Jin through puzzles?

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.100
How do you explain the “mirrors”?

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.040
If you view puzzles with fear in your 
eyes, they will seem terrifying.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:55.880
If you try to find the truth, 
the puzzle will show it to you.

00:20:56.790 --> 00:21:00.210
Don’t make that up and then 
say that’s how Jin feels!

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:02.210
Right. It’s the same 
as what you’re doing.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:07.430
There is still so much that you, me 
and Kaito don’t know about Jin.

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.870
Yeah. We really should 
work together to uncover--

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:14.630
Cut the crap! I know all about Jin!

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:16.130
That’s good enough!

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:19.530
Then we’ll have to do it without her.

00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:22.080
I swear that I will solve the hard,

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:25.970
complex puzzle hidden 
within Jin’s past.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:29.200
You’re free to try.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:34.220
After all, Jin’s going 
to be leaving with me.

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:45.360
Jin, I came to get you!

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.740
Come on. We can go together now.

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:55.250
I’m sorry. I can’t accompany you.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:56.790
Why not?

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:01.530
You’re... missing something.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:06.050
For some odd reason, I can’t 
help but get that feeling.

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:08.050
I’m sorry.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:15.480
Again... You said it again...

00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:21.480
You’re missing something.

00:24:02.350 --> 00:24:05.380
What an adorable black 
cat! What’s its name?

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:06.900
I never gave it one.

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:10.840
Then I’ll think one up! You’d 
like a cute name, right?

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:14.700
Oh, how’s Luna? Jiji?

00:24:15.490 --> 00:24:16.620
Or Tango?

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:17.870
Which do you like?

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:27.970
Rae-Rae is a Feline Friend

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:20.620
Next time, “Rae-Rae 
is a Feline Friend.”

00:24:20.620 --> 00:24:22.790
I’ll name it Jinko Makata.

00:24:23.380 --> 00:24:26.190
How cute--er, wait! What?

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Why am I included in this...? 
Octopus! Not quite, Rook! 
 We?e fried octy! Fried octy!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
